WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.127
- My ankle hurt. I don't have a contract.

00:00:02.127 --> 00:00:05.171
Coach Coughlin, he end up fining me and all type of shit. 

00:00:05.171 --> 00:00:06.423
I missed the whole preseason. 

00:00:06.423 --> 00:00:09.009
The game started at 7:00. I'm not playing. 

00:00:09.009 --> 00:00:11.636
I was at home, and my phone rings. 

00:00:11.636 --> 00:00:14.055
They said, "Plaxico, we got your contract done."

00:00:14.055 --> 00:00:16.683
I walked in the locker room. I put on my uniform. 

00:00:16.683 --> 00:00:19.936
Ten catches and 133 yards, and I hadn't played since the Super Bowl.

00:00:19.936 --> 00:00:26.026
♪♪♪ 

00:00:27.152 --> 00:00:28.903
- So who we got in the pool hall today?

00:00:28.903 --> 00:00:31.948
Oh, we got big Plax in the building. Plaxico Burress. What's good, baby?

00:00:31.948 --> 00:00:34.826
- I'm living pretty good, man.
Enjoying the retired life a little bit

00:00:34.826 --> 00:00:35.493
- Yeah, that's right.

00:00:35.493 --> 00:00:36.745
You nice on the sticks, or what's up?

00:00:36.745 --> 00:00:38.663
- I ain't too bad. How much money we got on the table?

00:00:38.663 --> 00:00:41.458
- Oh, how much money? Hold up, wait a minute.

00:00:41.458 --> 00:00:44.294
- When the money goes on the table, I get a lot better.
- We gonna play 10 a ball? What's up?

00:00:44.294 --> 00:00:45.754
- Oh, we’d get a lot better.
- What's up?

00:00:45.754 --> 00:00:46.379
-  I'll take the wallet.

00:00:46.379 --> 00:00:47.756
- [Laughing]

00:00:47.756 --> 00:00:48.715
We'll see how it plays out.

00:00:48.715 --> 00:00:49.632
- I'm ready when you ready.

00:00:49.632 --> 00:00:50.884
- All right, go ahead. Break it real quick then.

00:00:53.928 --> 00:00:55.930
So, Plax, you were known to play through injuries, right?

00:00:55.930 --> 00:00:56.556
- Right.

00:00:56.556 --> 00:00:59.476
- 2007, you're with the Giants,
and they win the Super Bowl that year. 

00:00:59.476 --> 00:01:00.101
- Right.

00:01:00.101 --> 00:01:01.728
- What happens before the season
with your ankle?

00:01:01.728 --> 00:01:04.981
- Well, in the offseason, I had some bone spurs removed from my left ankle.

00:01:04.981 --> 00:01:08.068
Going into the training camp, I just jumped up for a pass over the middle.

00:01:08.068 --> 00:01:13.656
Subconsciously in my mind, I didn't wanna put my left ankle down because, 
you know, it was still a little tender from the surgery.

00:01:13.656 --> 00:01:14.491
- Absolutely.

00:01:14.491 --> 00:01:18.620
- So I just come down, and I just put all my weight on my right foot, 

00:01:18.620 --> 00:01:21.623
and I just hear, like, a little “pop,” and I just thought I just, you know—

00:01:21.623 --> 00:01:22.624
- On the right one?

00:01:22.624 --> 00:01:23.625
- Yeah, on my right one.

00:01:23.625 --> 00:01:26.086
I tried to run and then cut; it hurts when I'm cutting.

00:01:26.086 --> 00:01:27.670
So I really don't know what's wrong.

00:01:27.670 --> 00:01:31.049
And so I end up missing the whole training camp, the whole preseason. 

00:01:31.049 --> 00:01:34.969
We get into the first game of the season against Dallas, and I have a good game.

00:01:34.969 --> 00:01:36.554
Eight catches, three touchdowns.

00:01:36.554 --> 00:01:37.764
- I'm a Cowboys fan. You ain't gotta rub it in.

00:01:37.764 --> 00:01:39.099
- Oh, man, I'mma rub it in all the way then. 

00:01:39.099 --> 00:01:39.682
- [Laughing]

00:01:39.682 --> 00:01:42.769
- So I think I had eight catches, 144 yards and three touchdowns.
- Aw, damn.

00:01:42.769 --> 00:01:44.270
- I think it was “Sunday Night Football.” 

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:46.272
So, yeah, so take that with you.

00:01:46.272 --> 00:01:47.315
- On two bad ankles?

00:01:47.315 --> 00:01:48.650
- On two bad ankles.

00:01:48.650 --> 00:01:52.070
- The following week, we’re playing against the Green Bay Packers at home.

00:01:52.070 --> 00:01:53.404
Al Harris is guarding me. 

00:01:53.404 --> 00:01:57.242
He steps on my foot, and it just [popping noise].

00:01:57.242 --> 00:02:00.537
And I heard, like, a crunch, like a [crunching noise]. 

00:02:00.537 --> 00:02:05.625
And that's when I kind of knew that the injury had went all the way south.

00:02:05.625 --> 00:02:10.922
I had a tendon that was completely snapped in half, with no stability in my foot or ankle. 

00:02:12.006 --> 00:02:13.591
And the following Monday, 

00:02:13.591 --> 00:02:16.845
I went upstairs to Jerry Reese, who was the general manager at the time, 

00:02:16.845 --> 00:02:18.930
and I'm like, "I can't perform the way that I want to.

00:02:18.930 --> 00:02:21.474
I can't push off my ankle. I can't push off of my foot.

00:02:21.474 --> 00:02:24.060
"We'll get some more tests, see what's really going on.” 

00:02:24.060 --> 00:02:29.816
So me and Ronnie Barnes, who was the head trainer for the Giants, 
we flew down to Charlotte, North Carolina, to see Dr. Bob Anderson. And—

00:02:29.816 --> 00:02:32.026
- Foot specialist that a lot of players see.
- Foot specialist, a lot of

00:02:32.026 --> 00:02:33.695
—well-respected, one of the best in the world.

00:02:33.695 --> 00:02:35.446
He was like, "You know, I can do three things. 

00:02:35.446 --> 00:02:38.116
No. 1, I can just put him in a cast for eight weeks, 

00:02:38.116 --> 00:02:42.036
but I'm afraid that if he's in a cast for eight weeks, when he comes out of the cast, 

00:02:42.036 --> 00:02:45.206
his leg is going to be so weak that he's not going to be able to perform anyway.

00:02:45.206 --> 00:02:48.084
No. 2, I can break his heel and reset it." 

00:02:48.084 --> 00:02:52.172
And when he said “break your heel,” I'm like, “Well, that's definitely not an option.

00:02:52.172 --> 00:02:54.966
I'm not just gonna let you break my foot on purpose.”

00:02:54.966 --> 00:03:00.805
So they wanted to break my heel and reset it and reattach the 
deltoid ligament that I had torn off the bone. 

00:03:00.805 --> 00:03:03.349
And it was like, “No. 3, he can simply just play. 

00:03:03.349 --> 00:03:07.187
It's gonna be based on his pain tolerance—how much pain, you know, he can take.”

00:03:07.187 --> 00:03:13.526
John Mara, who's the owner, and Ronnie Barnes, they were like, 
"Do you think you can go out and play on Sundays 

00:03:13.526 --> 00:03:14.903
and not practice?"

00:03:14.903 --> 00:03:16.404
- So you'd be on the field once a week, 

00:03:16.404 --> 00:03:17.071
game days.

00:03:17.071 --> 00:03:18.573
- Yeah, just once a week, just on Sunday.

00:03:18.573 --> 00:03:21.242
- And we know football's so predicated on practice.

00:03:21.242 --> 00:03:23.912
- Yeah, it's one of those things, it’s—nobody had ever done it.

00:03:23.912 --> 00:03:26.247
And when they asked me the question, I was like, 

00:03:26.247 --> 00:03:28.333
“I don't know. I'll give it a try.” 

00:03:28.333 --> 00:03:32.545
And in the back of my mind, I was like, “I'm putting my career on the line for the team.”

00:03:32.545 --> 00:03:35.173
As the season goes on, I go out and play. 

00:03:35.173 --> 00:03:38.343
My teammates have no idea why I'm not practicing.

00:03:39.552 --> 00:03:42.138
- What'd they think, it was like a vet privilege that you had or something?
- Yeah, yeah.

00:03:42.138 --> 00:03:44.682
Everybody was like, “Oh, man, you found a loophole in the system.” 

00:03:44.682 --> 00:03:45.683
I couldn't tell anybody.

00:03:45.683 --> 00:03:46.517
- Yeah.

00:03:46.517 --> 00:03:49.854
- And the owner and the trainer, they never spoke about it in the media. 

00:03:49.854 --> 00:03:54.067
Eli and myself, we spent a lot of time together when I wasn't playing. 

00:03:54.067 --> 00:03:58.947
I was playing some of the best football in my life, and I kinda 
attribute that to my ankle was in a lot of pain,

00:03:58.947 --> 00:04:00.782
but my legs were fresh on Sunday.

00:04:00.782 --> 00:04:01.616
- How was that dynamic?

00:04:01.616 --> 00:04:06.579
- A lot of times, he would give me signals, and the team had no idea 
what was going on. 

00:04:06.579 --> 00:04:12.502
It was just me and him on the same page based off of what we 
saw on film and how the guy was playing me.

00:04:12.502 --> 00:04:14.337
- What was some of his signals? What do you remember from that?

00:04:14.337 --> 00:04:18.258
- Oh, man, it was, like, you know, behind the back, down the leg for double seam. 

00:04:18.258 --> 00:04:19.884
It was, like, slant K. 

00:04:19.884 --> 00:04:22.762
You know, when I got into the red zone, he would give me the head nod.

00:04:22.762 --> 00:04:27.433
I was running the slant, and when he gave me the “no,” I was running the fade. 

00:04:27.433 --> 00:04:32.605
Kevin Gilbride, who was our offensive coordinator, he was like, 
"Man, what the hell was that? What did you just do?"

00:04:32.605 --> 00:04:35.817
I was like, "Hey, man, Eli gave me the slant signal, so I ran a slant.” 

00:04:35.817 --> 00:04:39.821
It's a first down. We broke a lot of rules. Nobody could really figure it out.

00:04:41.114 --> 00:04:41.864
- Oh, shit.

00:04:41.864 --> 00:04:42.740
- Uh-oh. 

00:04:42.740 --> 00:04:44.909
Things are getting real competitive real quick.

00:04:44.909 --> 00:04:46.327
- How are you playing through this injury though? 

00:04:46.327 --> 00:04:49.289
Like, how are you finding the energy and the effort to play through this?

00:04:49.289 --> 00:04:50.206
- You know, I really don't know. 

00:04:50.206 --> 00:04:53.835
I would wake up on Monday mornings, and my ankle would 
probably be, like, this big around, 

00:04:53.835 --> 00:04:56.671
and it was just trying to get to the next Sunday.

00:04:56.671 --> 00:05:05.346
Get the swelling down, get me off my feet and just get it to the point to where 
I could just bear the pain just to play into the following Sunday.

00:05:05.346 --> 00:05:06.306
- That's incredible, man. 

00:05:06.306 --> 00:05:10.393
So the ankle injury bothered you all season. Still, you have your career year though.

00:05:10.393 --> 00:05:11.102
- Right.

00:05:11.102 --> 00:05:13.187
- Numbers-wise, what do you end up doing in the regular season? Do you remember?

00:05:13.187 --> 00:05:17.734
- I think I had, like, 70 catches, 1,000 yards and 12 touchdowns. 

00:05:17.734 --> 00:05:20.028
And when I didn't make the Pro Bowl, I was pissed. 

00:05:20.028 --> 00:05:20.987
- Why?

00:05:20.987 --> 00:05:26.284
- Talking about cats who practice every day and didn't put up the numbers that I put up. 

00:05:26.284 --> 00:05:29.787
It pissed me off so bad that when I got to the playoffs, I took it up another level. 

00:05:29.787 --> 00:05:31.080
- Talk to me: What happened in the playoffs?

00:05:31.080 --> 00:05:33.916
- Oh, man, we just smoked everybody in front of us. 

00:05:33.916 --> 00:05:37.211
Straight up. I was mad, man. That shit pissed me off, man. 

00:05:38.504 --> 00:05:42.508
The week of the Super Bowl, I come out of the shower and slip, 

00:05:42.508 --> 00:05:44.635
and I, like, catch myself. 

00:05:44.635 --> 00:05:47.096
Maybe I, you know, kinda twisted my knee a little bit. 

00:05:47.096 --> 00:05:52.727
And I turn on the lights, and I look at my knee, and my knee is, like, 
swollen all the way around.

00:05:52.727 --> 00:05:57.148
I got the ankle and the MCL all on one damn leg.

00:05:57.148 --> 00:06:00.735
Fast-forward to Sunday, they wrap my knee up. 

00:06:00.735 --> 00:06:03.279
They give me some really, really, really good medicine.

00:06:03.279 --> 00:06:04.739
- [Laughing] 

00:06:04.739 --> 00:06:06.699
What, Tora, or you know what you was on?

00:06:06.699 --> 00:06:07.742
- Oh, man, I don't know what it was. 

00:06:07.742 --> 00:06:08.618
- [Laughing]

00:06:08.618 --> 00:06:10.953
- Even if I knew what it was, I wouldn't say nothing. 

00:06:10.953 --> 00:06:12.997
But, man,

00:06:12.997 --> 00:06:14.040
I didn't have a knee.

00:06:14.749 --> 00:06:16.250
- You had to do what you had to do, man.

00:06:16.250 --> 00:06:19.962
- Man, I felt like I had bought a knee off eBay or something.

00:06:19.962 --> 00:06:22.048
I was feeling fantastic.

00:06:22.048 --> 00:06:24.967
So fast-forward to the game, to the fourth quarter.

00:06:24.967 --> 00:06:27.220
- At this point too, how's your knee feeling? How's your ankle feeling?

00:06:27.220 --> 00:06:29.430
- I'm saying to myself, I said, “You know what, man? 

00:06:29.430 --> 00:06:32.433
My knee's killing me.” I said, You know what? It's a Super Bowl.

00:06:32.433 --> 00:06:36.396
If I gotta jump off of this leg like it's not hurting, 

00:06:36.396 --> 00:06:39.440
if I tear my knee up, then fuck it.” 

00:06:40.149 --> 00:06:42.318
And the ball couldn't come down fast enough. 

00:06:42.318 --> 00:06:46.781
And I was just saying to myself, I said, “Man, if you drop this football, 

00:06:47.073 --> 00:06:49.617
you will not be allowed back in New Jersey.”

00:06:49.617 --> 00:06:51.244
- [Laughing]

00:06:51.577 --> 00:06:57.208
- Still to this day, even as time goes on, it starts to mean even more to you.

00:06:57.208 --> 00:07:00.461
- Antonio Pierce is over there at ASU now. Go Devils. 

00:07:00.461 --> 00:07:03.423
He said you sacrificed your future earnings 

00:07:03.423 --> 00:07:05.883
that season with what you did.

00:07:05.883 --> 00:07:06.843
- I did.

00:07:06.843 --> 00:07:11.681
- Were the players respecting kind of what you were doing as they 
started to find out what it took for you to be on the field?

00:07:11.681 --> 00:07:17.145
- I think later on they started to understand the severity of my injury. 

00:07:17.145 --> 00:07:20.690
But, you know, I put it all on the line for myself and them. 

00:07:20.690 --> 00:07:25.611
After that season, I did not work out or run for, like, six whole months.

00:07:25.611 --> 00:07:26.446
- After the Super Bowl?

00:07:26.446 --> 00:07:28.698
- I couldn't run. I didn't run nowhere. 

00:07:28.698 --> 00:07:32.910
I said, “Man, I'mma take this time off to heal up and to get myself better 

00:07:32.910 --> 00:07:35.538
so I can go out and play, you know, for the season.”

00:07:37.999 --> 00:07:38.749
- Stayin’ in my zone

00:07:38.749 --> 00:07:40.418
- Man, this boy been practicing.

00:07:40.418 --> 00:07:41.377
- [Laughing]

00:07:41.377 --> 00:07:44.172
- Knowing he was gonna be shooting pool on this show.

